    "article_summary": "The article describes a photoinduced radical sulfur dioxide insertion strategy combined with an asymmetric Truce-Smiles rearrangement to synthesize chiral sulfones containing quaternary carbon stereocenters. Two complementary systems using aryldiazonium salts or thianthrenium salts as radical precursors were developed, utilizing visible light photoredox catalysis to achieve high stereospecificity and broad functional group tolerance.",
